WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.220
Caroline Aghajanian: On this
episode of "Travel Dares":

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:11.157
I'm taking Nico to La Grande Fistoire,

00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:14.459
where were gonna cross a
200-foot suspension bridge.

00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:16.675
Whoo! Oh, my God!

00:00:16.675 --> 00:00:18.040
No, no!

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.430
Nico Reyes: And I'm taking Caroline to

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.680
Savonnerie Marseillaise de la Licorne,

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:23.750
where we're gonna learn how soap is made.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:25.270
Caroline: Come join us on our adventures

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.936
on this episode of "Travel Dares."

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:34.350
This is "Travel Dares,"

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:37.240
the show where we do daring
activities all over Europe,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:40.080
empowered by my Marriott
Bonvoy Boundless card.

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.670
In this episode, Nico and I
are in the south of France.

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.210
Nico, how are you doing?

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:48.330
Nico: I am so psyched! I'm
really excited to be here.

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:50.130
I've always wanted to come
to the south of France,

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.670
and I can't wait to get started.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:53.763
Caroline: Yes! So, here
is your first clue.

00:00:53.763 --> 00:00:55.440
Nico: Hand it over!

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.277
OK.

00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:00.283
I have no idea what that could mean.

00:01:00.283 --> 00:01:02.570
Caroline: You're just
gonna have to find out.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:06.550
Nico: It's definitely gonna
be something, like, active.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.350
Either, like, maybe climbing, running.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:12.830
Best foot forward? That's
where my mind goes.

00:01:12.830 --> 00:01:14.650
Caroline: A via ferrata
is a climbing route

00:01:14.650 --> 00:01:17.990
using steel cables that
hikers secure themselves to.

00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:20.640
They're super popular
among European hikers,

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.572
and this one happens to have

00:01:22.572 --> 00:01:24.953
a super scary bridge right in the middle.

00:01:24.953 --> 00:01:26.980
Nico, I'm so excited for you!
Nico: I know!

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:28.820
I wanna rip this blindfold off.

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.970
Caroline: OK, we're almost
there, just a few more steps.

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:31.803
Nico: OK.

00:01:31.803 --> 00:01:33.460
Caroline: Take your blindfold off,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.710
because we are walking across that bridge!

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:37.950
Nico: No, we're not!

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:38.893
Caroline: Yes, we are!

00:01:39.791 --> 00:01:42.092
Nico: Oh, my God!

00:01:42.092 --> 00:01:44.009
That is so high!

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.010
Caroline: OK, we're hiking up now.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:01:59.670
We have about a 15-minute hike

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.360
until we actually get to the bridge.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.410
Nico: I was half right about my clue.

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:06.150
'Cause we are hiking it up.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.245
Caroline: We are. We're
doing something active.

00:02:08.245 --> 00:02:10.889
Nico: I always wanted to
be a little more athletic.

00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:13.010
And we're building so much muscle!

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.333
Caroline: Oh, we're
getting really steep here.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.420
I'm climbing.

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:20.293
There's no more trail, so
we're just going on rocks now.

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:22.370
I'm scared.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:23.203
Nico: All right, so, we're about

00:02:23.203 --> 00:02:26.270
to go on the bridge! Finally. We made it!

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:28.760
Caroline: It's taken...this
was not 15 minutes,

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:30.510
let me tell you that.

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:37.990
Oh, boy!

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.043
Oh, my God!

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:46.830
Nico: I will never, oh, my God!

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:48.100
Caroline: Oh, God!

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.400
Nico: You got this, Caroline.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:50.325
Caroline: My arms are shaking.

00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:52.380
Please, please, can we go faster?

00:02:52.380 --> 00:02:53.550
Nico, are you OK?

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:54.383
Nico: I'm good.

00:02:54.383 --> 00:02:55.580
OK, I'm OK.

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:56.563
I'm nervous.

00:02:56.563 --> 00:02:58.340
Caroline: Oh, my God,
oh, my God, oh, my God.

00:02:58.340 --> 00:02:59.280
I'm on the bridge.

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.260
Nico: Oh, God!

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.170
OK, Caroline.
Caroline: Hi.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:03.003
Nico: I'm sorry.

00:03:03.003 --> 00:03:03.836
Caroline: It's OK. Just come on.

00:03:03.836 --> 00:03:05.742
Nico: Hello, hello,
hello, hello, hello. OK.

00:03:05.742 --> 00:03:07.540
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:09.232
OK, we're on the bridge.

00:03:09.232 --> 00:03:11.099
[Nico exhales]
Chandra: On the right side.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:15.863
Caroline: How are you doing, Nico?

00:03:15.863 --> 00:03:18.560
Nico: I'm good, this is incredible!

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:19.640
Caroline: Oh my God!

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:21.900
Nico: The view. It's so...
Caroline: I am terrified,

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.530
but I've never felt more
confident in my life!

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.301
Nico: The air up here is incredible!

00:03:28.301 --> 00:03:30.280
Whoa, it does make me a little bit

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.763
nervous when the wind blows!

00:03:32.763 --> 00:03:34.528
[Caroline screams]
Nico: Oh, my God!

00:03:34.528 --> 00:03:37.273
Caroline: The wind, the wind!
Nico: Oh, no, no, no, no!

00:03:37.273 --> 00:03:39.790
Caroline: Nico, are you OK?

00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:42.421
Nico: Caroline, this wind is really bad.

00:03:42.421 --> 00:03:44.729
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:03:44.729 --> 00:03:46.220
[Caroline breathes heavily]

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.053
You're OK!

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:49.588
Nico, you got this! Let's sing a song.

00:03:49.588 --> 00:03:50.838
La, la, la, la.

00:03:51.950 --> 00:03:53.680
Nico: I feel like, for
something that scared

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:58.080
me so much just to get to,
I'm smiling a whole lot.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:00.650
'Cause this is, like, once in a lifetime.

00:04:00.650 --> 00:04:03.160
I'm never gonna have this view again.

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.665
I'm never gonna be this
on top of the world again.

00:04:05.665 --> 00:04:07.362
"Travel Dares"!

00:04:07.362 --> 00:04:11.318
Both: "Travel Dares"! "Travel Dares"!

00:04:11.318 --> 00:04:13.960
Nico: No one can ever say
anything to me ever again.

00:04:13.960 --> 00:04:17.420
I am the bravest woman alive,
and I don't care what you say!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.730
Caroline: We made it!

00:04:18.730 --> 00:04:20.970
Nico: Now that we did it,
Caroline, I feel really good.

00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:22.200
Caroline: I do feel good.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.010
Nico: We just did that!

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:25.280
Caroline: We did that!

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:26.549
Nico: We did that!

00:04:26.549 --> 00:04:27.407
Whoo!

00:04:27.407 --> 00:04:28.770
Chandra: Congratulations!

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:30.953
Nico: Oh, God, that was intense.

00:04:31.858 --> 00:04:34.410
Caroline: Rocks! Oh, my God, rocks!

00:04:34.410 --> 00:04:36.769
Nico: The rocks are
comforting to Caroline.

00:04:36.769 --> 00:04:39.201
Caroline: You guys, we
made it! Nico, we made it!

00:04:39.201 --> 00:04:40.100
[cheering]

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.062
Nico: I'm freaking proud of us!

00:04:42.062 --> 00:04:44.580
Caroline: I am so proud!

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:47.163
That was the wildest thing I've ever done!

00:04:47.163 --> 00:04:50.913
All right, Nico, now let's
get off this mountain.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:54.370
Nico: I cannot believe we survived that.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:56.020
Caroline: I know, Nico, that was probably

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:57.330
one of the hardest dares we've done.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.030
But you absolutely killed it.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:04:59.960
I'm so proud of you!

00:04:59.960 --> 00:05:00.793
Nico: Thank you!

00:05:00.793 --> 00:05:02.130
I hope I can say the same about

00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:03.350
you when it comes to my dare.

00:05:03.350 --> 00:05:06.008
Caroline: OK, well let's
see what your clue is.

00:05:08.690 --> 00:05:10.520
OK!
Nico: What are you thinking?

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:13.410
Caroline: A spa day, most likely.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:15.058
Nico: Let's hope.
Caroline: OK!

00:05:15.058 --> 00:05:15.950
[laughing]

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:16.950
Caroline: The first thing that...

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.683
oh, wait.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.120
Wait a minute.

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:23.233
I feel like we're making soap.

00:05:24.217 --> 00:05:25.550
I feel like that's what we're gonna do.

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:26.700
We're gonna make soap.

00:05:26.700 --> 00:05:28.510
Something in the beauty world.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:30.010
Um, I don't know, and we're also

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.080
gonna integrate lavender in this somehow.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:33.913
That's what I think.

00:05:33.913 --> 00:05:34.746
Nico: Walk, walk, walk, walk, walk.

00:05:34.746 --> 00:05:35.579
[Caroline cheers]

00:05:35.579 --> 00:05:37.460
Caroline: It smells good!

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:39.830
Nico: Stand right there
and stick your hand out.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:41.115
Caroline: Stick my hand.

00:05:41.115 --> 00:05:42.515
Nico: What do you think that is?

00:05:43.450 --> 00:05:45.541
Caroline: It's soap!

00:05:45.541 --> 00:05:46.564
Nico: Take off your blindfold.

00:05:46.564 --> 00:05:49.466
We're making soap today!
Caroline: We're making soap?!

00:05:49.466 --> 00:05:50.900
Oh, my God!

00:05:50.900 --> 00:05:51.733
Nico: Look at this place!

00:05:51.733 --> 00:05:55.999
Caroline: Oh, my God,
this is like soap heaven!

00:06:05.567 --> 00:06:06.770
Caroline and Nico: Bonjour Jerome!

00:06:06.770 --> 00:06:08.005
Jerome Monge: Bonjour, nice to meet you.

00:06:08.005 --> 00:06:09.280
Caroline: Thank you for having us!

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.780
What are we doing today?

00:06:10.780 --> 00:06:13.279
Jerome: We are making lavender soap today.

00:06:13.279 --> 00:06:15.640
Caroline: Lavender.
Nico: I love lavender.

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.130
The smell of lavender soap is so good.

00:06:17.130 --> 00:06:18.260
Caroline: Yes!

00:06:18.260 --> 00:06:21.270
Jerome: It is in this machine
where there is initial mix

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:24.890
between oil and soda. Soda
is a sodium hydroxide.

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.780
Because all the soap are made with

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.390
this soap mix: fat and soda.

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:32.480
And, here, there is the
little pieces of soap.

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.322
We are going to put in this machine.

00:06:34.322 --> 00:06:36.682
Caroline: Whoo!
[Nico laughs]

00:06:36.682 --> 00:06:38.298
Soap pebbles!

00:06:40.397 --> 00:06:42.020
Nico: Is our soap coming out?

00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.303
Caroline: I see it, I see it!
Nico: Oh, there it goes!

00:06:45.303 --> 00:06:47.970
Caroline: This is so mesmerizing.

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.848
Nico: We make some pretty beautiful soap.

00:06:49.848 --> 00:06:51.561
Caroline: I know, this is fantastic.

00:06:51.561 --> 00:06:54.420
Jerome: And after, when we
have this paper of soap,

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.120
we are going to put it in this mixer.

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:59.147
And after, we are going to prepare, right,

00:06:59.147 --> 00:07:01.860
the perfume and the color
to put in this machine.

00:07:01.860 --> 00:07:03.850
Nico: Caroline, I'm gonna
press the green button again,

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:05.110
and you start pouring.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.455
Caroline: You got it.

00:07:06.455 --> 00:07:07.288
Nico: Oh!

00:07:08.791 --> 00:07:09.962
The purple's coming!

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.196
Caroline: Wow!

00:07:11.196 --> 00:07:12.380
Nico: Look at that!

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.813
This feels like our soap
is finally coming to life!

00:07:14.813 --> 00:07:17.487
Caroline: I know, our
little baby's being born!

00:07:17.487 --> 00:07:19.020
Nico: Our lavender soap!

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:20.070
Caroline: That's a more essential oil.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.797
Nico: Oh, the smell's hitting me again.

00:07:22.797 --> 00:07:25.782
Jerome: And this machine can transform

00:07:25.782 --> 00:07:29.283
the flakes of soap in tagliatelle of soap.

00:07:29.283 --> 00:07:30.116
Nico: Pasta!

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:30.949
Jerome: You make pasta of soap.

00:07:30.949 --> 00:07:32.410
It's the same machine to make pasta.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.110
It's good.
Caroline and Nico: Oh!

00:07:35.110 --> 00:07:36.197
Nico: Oh, my God!

00:07:36.197 --> 00:07:37.395
Caroline: Oh, my God!

00:07:37.395 --> 00:07:38.524
Nico: That does look like pasta.

00:07:38.524 --> 00:07:40.320
Caroline: It is pasta!

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:41.837
Jerome: Next, you are going to take

00:07:41.837 --> 00:07:45.170
this tagliatelle of
soap to compact the soap

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:46.824
to give the final shape to soap.

00:07:46.824 --> 00:07:48.300
Nico: Ready, Caroline?
Caroline: Ready!

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.781
Nico: Let's see our soap.

00:07:50.781 --> 00:07:53.025
Both: It's coming out!

00:07:53.025 --> 00:07:54.190
Caroline: Here it comes!

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.023
It's like a long snake.

00:07:56.877 --> 00:07:58.462
Jerome: Cut and use our tang.

00:07:58.462 --> 00:07:59.324
And you....

00:07:59.324 --> 00:08:00.793
Nico: You made a bar of soap!

00:08:00.793 --> 00:08:02.823
Caroline: I made a bar of soap!

00:08:02.823 --> 00:08:03.656
Jerome: That's good.

00:08:03.656 --> 00:08:05.017
Caroline: One, two!

00:08:05.017 --> 00:08:05.850
Oh.

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:06.683
Jerome: Stronger, be very strong.

00:08:06.683 --> 00:08:07.600
[Nico laughs]

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.441
Or you can stamp two timers,
so if the first one go....

00:08:09.441 --> 00:08:10.274
Caroline: Oh, two times,

00:08:10.274 --> 00:08:11.524
like pound it two times.
Nico: That may be better.

00:08:11.524 --> 00:08:12.770
Caroline: One here, one here maybe?

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:13.610
Jerome: Yes.
Caroline: OK, I'ma do that.

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:14.443
Boom! Boom!

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:16.534
Nico: That one's good!

00:08:16.534 --> 00:08:18.490
That one is really good!

00:08:18.490 --> 00:08:19.980
Jerome: And after, you push.

00:08:21.072 --> 00:08:22.405
Caroline and Nico: Oh!

00:08:23.805 --> 00:08:25.521
Nico: It's gonna be loud, I'm scared.

00:08:28.090 --> 00:08:30.490
It's, like, screeching.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:32.603
Take the excess off.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:34.617
Is it coming out on its own?

00:08:34.617 --> 00:08:35.450
Ew!

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.283
That was weird.

00:08:36.283 --> 00:08:37.680
That was so weird!

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:38.513
Caroline: Oh, my God, Nico,

00:08:38.513 --> 00:08:39.346
these are gonna make such great gifts!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.920
And we get to tell everybody
we helped make them!

00:08:42.920 --> 00:08:44.420
Little soapmakers.

00:08:49.834 --> 00:08:51.180
We've been to Northern France,

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.346
and now we're in the south of France,

00:08:52.346 --> 00:08:53.469
and they're both so different.

00:08:53.469 --> 00:08:55.950
Like, they both have their
own unique charm to it.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:56.910
Nico: Yeah, I agree.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:08:58.450
I definitely loved experiencing

00:08:58.450 --> 00:09:01.020
the culture around here.
And the croissants.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.650
Caroline: Nico, are you
ready for your rating?

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:03.483
Nico: Yes!

00:09:03.483 --> 00:09:06.330
Caroline: OK, so, I have
to say, this is probably

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.998
one of the hardest dares
we've ever done on this show.

00:09:08.998 --> 00:09:12.482
We had to climb up that
challenging mountain,

00:09:12.482 --> 00:09:15.910
and then we scaled down to
get to the super-scary bridge.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:19.400
And I'm so impressed of how
well you handled yourself.

00:09:19.400 --> 00:09:22.050
So I'm giving you five out of five stars.

00:09:22.050 --> 00:09:24.420
Nico: Yes!
Caroline: I'd give a 10

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:26.149
if I could, Nico!
Nico: Oh, my gosh!

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:27.080
Caroline: It was so good!

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:30.110
Nico: Five on my first
dare ever. I'm so psyched!

00:09:30.110 --> 00:09:30.943
Caroline: You deserve it.
Nico: Thank you,

00:09:30.943 --> 00:09:31.776
thank you, thank you, thank you!

00:09:31.776 --> 00:09:32.609
Caroline.
Caroline: Yes.

00:09:32.609 --> 00:09:35.110
Nico: I was expecting
you to love soapmaking,

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.610
just because you're a huge
fan of everything beauty.

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:40.430
You were working that
soap-slicing machine like a champ!

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:41.263
No fear that your fingers
could be chopped off

00:09:41.263 --> 00:09:42.096
at any moment.

00:09:43.580 --> 00:09:45.857
And for that, I will give you

00:09:45.857 --> 00:09:46.773
one,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:48.933
two,

00:09:50.102 --> 00:09:50.935
three,

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:52.893
four,

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.163
five.
Caroline: Yes!

00:09:57.040 --> 00:09:59.380
Five lavender stars!

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:00.990
Nico: You did a really, really good job.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:01.988
Caroline: Thank you so much.

00:10:01.988 --> 00:10:03.816
They still smell so good!

00:10:03.816 --> 00:10:04.740
Thank you so much.

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:06.060
Nico, this was so much fun.

